ovbeg()
{

	if (!value(OPEN))
		error("Can't use open/visual unless open option is set");
	if (inopen)
		error("Recursive open/visual not allowed");
	Vlines = lineDOL();
	fixzero();
	setdot();
	pastwh();
	dot = addr2;
}

ovend(f)
	ttymode f;
{

	splitw++;
	vgoto(WECHO, 0);
	vclreol();
	vgoto(WECHO, 0);
	holdcm = 0;
	splitw = 0;
	ostop(f);
rations in visual now wrap around line boundaries.
Thus a sequence of enough \fBw\fR commands will get to any word after the
current position in the file, and \fBb\fR's will back up to any
previous position.  Thus these are more like the sentence operations
.I (
and
.I ) .
(You still can't back around line boundaries during inserts however.)
.IP 2.3
The
.I /
and
.I ?
searches now find the next or previous instance of the searched for string.
Previously, they would not find strings on the current line.
Thus ndicate the beginning and ending lines before the write command,
for example
.DS I 1i
:\|\fB45,$w ending
.R
.DE
Here all lines from 45 through the end of the buffer
are written onto the file named
.I ending.
The lines remain in the buffer
as part of the document you are editing,
and you may continue to edit the entire buffer.
.SH
Recovering files
.PP
Under most circumstances,
edit's crash recovery mechanism
is able to save work to within a few lines of changes
after a crash or if the phone is hung up accide	setoutt();
	undvis();
	COLUMNS = OCOLUMNS;
	inopen = 0;
	flusho();
	netchHAD(Vlines);
}

