/*
 * Ex version 3
 * Mark Horton, UCB
 * Bill Joy UCB
 *
 * Open and visual mode definitions.
 * 
 * There are actually 4 major states in open/visual modes.  These
 * are visual, crt open (where the cursor can move about the screen and
 * the screen can scroll and be erased), one line open (on dumb glass-crt's
 * like the adm3), and hardcopy open (for everything else).
 *
 * The basic state is given b.tr ||
.TH TERMCAP 5 5/10/80 5
.UC 4
.SH NAME
termcap \- terminal capability data base
.SH SYNOPSIS
/etc/termcap
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Termcap
is a data base describing terminals,
used,
.IR e.g. ,
by
.IR vi (1)
and
.IR curses (3).
Terminals are described in
.I termcap
by giving a set of capabilities which they have, and by describing
how operations are performed.
Padding requirements and initialization sequences
are included in
.I termcap.
.PP
Entries in
.I termcap
consist of a number of `:' separated fields.
